      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U2", "U3"],
      "pins": ["U2.1", "U2.5", "U2.6", "U2.7", "U2.8", "U3.1", "U3.5", "U3.6", "U3.7", "U3.8"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "GND", "RST", "SDA", "PWM", "SCK"],
      "observed": "Two microcontrollers, an ATtiny45 (U2) and an ATtiny13V (U3), have their supply, reset, and corresponding I/O pins connected to the same nets. For example, both PB1 pins are on PWM, both PB2 pins are on SCK, and both PB0 pins are on SDA.",
      "expected": "A controller design should have one MCU driving these shared signals, or explicitly isolate/select the MCU if the two devices are alternatives. The specification describes an ATtiny-driven fan controller, not two controllers operating in parallel.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"9\") (name \"PWM\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"11\") (name \"SCK\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PB2\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PB2\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both MCUs are populated, they can drive shared I/O nets simultaneously and contend, while executing independently. If they are intended as assembly alternatives, that selection is not represented in the provided design files.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design directly connects Q2's base-emitter junction across VCC and GND with no current limiting, a likely damaging fault. It also connects two different MCU devices in parallel across shared control and I/O nets."
}

